      "without_skill_failures": [
        "States IdentityServer has no built-in HSM/KMS provider and a custom ISigningKeyStore does not give non-exportable keys",
        "Subclasses DefaultTokenCreationService and overrides CreateJwtAsync to call the KMS async sign API, registering it as ITokenCreationService",
        "Registers the KMS public key as the signing credential with AddSigningCredential and disables automatic key management (KeyManagement.Enabled = false)",
        "Takes alg and kid from the registered signing credential so the header matches discovery/JWKS",
        "Notes SAML signing does not go through ITokenCreationService and requires a private key, so this approach doesn't cover SAML",
        "Mentions rotation is the developer's responsibility (publish new key via AddValidationKey ahead of time) and each token costs a KMS call"
      ]
    },
